# readiness gap — the wall shell versus the continuous derivation (spec/readiness-recovery ac-5)
# This is a GAP LIST, not parity. The post-design workbench lane consumes it; a change here must be deliberate.
# Derived on the claim-wall fixture with the design bridge wired (R-RR1-20); families neither side emits on that fixture are not listed.
# Fixture: the claim-wall Go fixture stands in for ac-5's e2e harness fixture (R-RR1-21, SI-209) because the harness provisioner is cmd/e2eharness's package main and unimportable from a Go test; families a side emits only under conditions this fixture lacks (for example shape/board needs an open sticky) are not listed, and the harness fixture's own gap is inherited unproven by the post-design workbench lane.
wall-only:
  context/agent-writes
  context/policy
  review/acceptance
  review/worktree
  success/criteria
loader-only:
  context/verdict
  review/action
  review/blocker/<id>
  review/eventual-derivation
  review/role/<id>
  shape/board
  shape/mutation
  shape/provenance
  success/contributor/<id>
